# Wild wheat (emmer, einkorn): golden stalks with stout, dense, upright ears and fanning awns a little
# shorter than the ear, in drifts on warm, dry grassland. Head Grain: Ear = the ear's kind (Dense / Slender / Panicle),
# one stalk per object (Petals is ignored), HeadSize = the ear, Open = how far it nods, Awns = their length (0..1 = 0 .. 2 x
# the ear). Color = the ear, Color2 = the straw. Format: Code/Procedural/CONTEXT.md, "Ground clutter".
ClutterType WildWheat
	Kind Flower
	Seed 301
	Scale 1.0 1.75
	Range 80
	Color 0.78 0.64 0.34
	Color2 0.72 0.66 0.42
	Head Grain
	Ear Dense
	Petals 4
	Open 5
	PetalWidth 0.3
	Stem 0.75
	HeadSize 0.14
	Awns 0.35
	Placement
		Density 0.2
		Temperature 8 26
		Precipitation 250 800
		Grass 0 1
		Canopy 1 0
		Cluster 14 0.1
		Slope 0.6
